                                    </span>
</a>
<br>
<br>
<span style=3D"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, V=
erdana, sans-serif;">
                                    Almost everyone agrees that AI policy s=
hould be evidence-based. However, science is often messy and full of caveat=
s, which doesn't fit well with policymakers' demands for clean answers. Man=
y AI benchmarks have saturated and can no longer give a clear 'no' on risks=
. Experiments show how much we still have to learn. We need to spend less t=
ime proving that today's AIs are safe and more time figuring out how to tel=
l if future AIs are dangerous.
                                </span>
</span>
</div>
